          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-02 22:18:56.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: parallelize sanity-sec 31 tunefs",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: parallelize sanity-sec 31 tunefs\n\ntest_31 and cleanup_31 run about 40 serial tunefs calls per pass,\nthree or more per target, each with its own ssh and a stop and\nwriteconf round trip.\n\nDo two tunefs per target, one to erase the old mgsnode and one to\nset the new one with writeconf, with the mds1 service node options\nin the same calls, on all targets in parallel. The two must stay\nseparate: on ZFS a key erased and set in one call is stored with a\nleading ':'. The parallel calls use parallel_start() with a new\nTUNEFS operation, so PARALLEL_OPS=0 or PARALLEL_TUNEFS=0 serializes\nthem. MMP is left enabled by the servicenode tunefs, as before.\n\ncleanup_31 restored an existing mds1 failover node with\n--servicenode, though the framework formats with --failnode, so\nmds1 was left with only its partner as a service node and could\nnot mount. Restore it with the option it was set with.\n\nOn a rocky9 ldiskfs cluster (1 MDS with 4 MDTs, 1 OSS with 4 OSTs,\n1 client), test 31 took 422s before and 400s after. At about 20s\nsaved per run and 6972 CI runs per 30 days, an estimate of roughly\n40 hours.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=31\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=31\nFixes: f70821fc1450 (\"LU-16775 tests: cleanup target after sanity-sec test_31\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Iaf833bb42bf91925e76f33775405fe8d753eee89\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
